<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Harjumaa</h1><p class="st-meta">800 CE – 1219 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Inland county of northern Estonia that fell to Denmark in 1219 and later launched the great St George's Night Uprising of 1343.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harju-county">Harjumaa</a>, inland from the coast around modern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/reval">Tallinn</a>, was one of the ancient Estonian lands, made up of several parishes with hillforts. It was closely linked to the coastal county of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ravala">Rävala</a>, and the two are often treated together in the sources.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Its elders led the free farmers in war and council. The district grew grain on limestone soils and traded through the harbour at Lindanise. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-of-livonia">Henry of Livonia</a> names <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harju-county">Harjumaa's</a> people among those who met for a common assembly at Raikküla.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the Danish victory at Lindanise in 1219, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harju-county">Harjumaa</a> passed under Danish rule and became part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-estonia-1219-1346">Duchy of Estonia</a> (1219-1346). In 1343 its peasants began the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/st-georges-night-uprising">St George's Night Uprising</a>, which was crushed by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/livonian-order">Livonian Order</a>, after which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> sold the duchy to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/harjumaa.jpg" alt="Harjumaa" width="320" height="200"><figcaption>Image: Diego Delso · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ayuntamiento,_vistas_panor%C3%A1micas_desde_Toompea,_Tallin,_Estonia,_2012-08-05,_DD_21.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>800 CE – 1219 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Estonian paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Estonian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/estonia">Estonia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Harria, Harju</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1010&amp;focus=harjumaa" aria-label="Harjumaa on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5207 184 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Harjumaa lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5527 440L5521 437"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5521 437h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5527 440h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5527 440h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1010&amp;focus=harjumaa">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
